#. type: Title #
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Contribute"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Code, bug reports, translations and tests with other cassettes are welcome."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Issues and pull requests on [GitHub](https://github.com/joshii-h/etiketto) are welcome, no Forgejo account needed. They are copied automatically to [Forgejo](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto), the main repository, with a link on GitHub. Review and merge happen there; your commits are kept, so GitHub shows the pull request as merged. The discussion can stay on GitHub.  With a Forgejo account you can contribute there directly.  Details: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**App translations**: `tools/strings_<lang>.py`, see CONTRIBUTING."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**This documentation**: `site/po/<lang>.po`, see [site/README.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/site/README.md).  Names of buttons and settings come from the app translation automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Other printers**: printing goes through a backend interface; a new printer is a new backend. The VC-500W protocol is described in [docs/protocol.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/docs/protocol.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Etiketto"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto designs and prints colour labels on the Brother VC-500W (ZINK paper)  under Linux, the counterpart to Brother's Color Label Editor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Main window](media/main.png#only-light)  ![Main window](media/main-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Text, images, QR codes and barcodes; backgrounds printed edge to edge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Preview at print resolution: what you see is what is printed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cassette detection, vivid colours and cut modes over the network"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "26 languages, follows the light or dark mode of the desktop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printers: Brother VC-500W (also sold as ColAura). Further printers can be added as a backend, see [Contribute](contribute.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Flathub is in preparation. Until then, build it yourself:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto.git && cd etiketto\n"
"flatpak install --user flathub org.gnome.Sdk//51 org.gnome.Platform//51\n"
"flatpak-builder --user --install --force-clean build-dir \\\n"
"    build-aux/flatpak/xyz.joshuahirsig.Etiketto.yml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "install.sh"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install the system packages, then run the script as your user (no root):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Distribution | Packages |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Debian, Ubuntu | `python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 gir1.2-adw-1 python3-gi-cairo python3-venv gettext` |\n"
"| Fedora | `python3-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python3-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Arch | `python-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Gentoo | `dev-python/pygobject gui-libs/gtk:4 gui-libs/libadwaita dev-python/pycairo sys-devel/gettext` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto.git && cd etiketto\n"
"./install.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Uninstall: `./install.sh --uninstall` or `flatpak uninstall xyz.joshuahirsig.Etiketto`.  Saved labels and templates are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch the printer on. Etiketto finds it in the network (Bonjour) and detects the inserted cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Not found? Enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]], e.g.  `VC-500W1234.local` or `192.168.1.50`. New printer: set up its Wi-Fi first, see [Printer](printer.md#wifi)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Add]] text, an image or a code, then [[ui:Print]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Save]] stores the label as `.etiketto` file, [[ui:Save as template…]] adds it to [[ui:Templates]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printer and troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wi-Fi setup { #wifi }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto does not set up Wi-Fi. Use a phone or the printer's web interface once:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Hold the Wi-Fi button until it turns from blue to white."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Connect phone or computer to the open network \"Brother VC-500W…\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open `https://192.168.0.1` (accept the certificate warning) or Brother's Color Label Editor app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose your network and enter the password. Only 2.4 GHz, WPA or open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Later, the web interface is at `https://` and the printer's address: \"Network Wi-Fi Setup\" changes the network (or \"click here\" to enter it by hand), \"AirPrint Options\" sets name, location and firmware updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cassettes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cassette | Width |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| CZ-1001 | 9 mm (3/8″) |\n"
"| CZ-1002 | 12 mm (1/2″) |\n"
"| CZ-1003 | 19 mm (3/4″) |\n"
"| CZ-1004 | 25 mm (1″) |\n"
"| CZ-1005 | 50 mm (2″) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto shows the inserted cassette, remaining tape, printable width, lot number and the presumed production date. ZINK paper ages: old paper prints paler and yellowish, Etiketto warns about old cassettes. Store cassettes cool and dry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cleaning: insert the cleaning cassette CK-1000, cleaning starts by itself.  Do it when stripes appear, or every 20 to 30 labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No printer found]]: printer on and in the same network? The search needs the Avahi service (installed on most desktops, any init system); systemd-resolved alone resolves `.local` names but cannot search. Otherwise enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer not reachable]]: check the address, the printer may have a new IP. Switch the printer off and on again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Wrong cassette]]: the label was designed for another width. Change [[ui:Tape width]] or the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No cassette inserted]] or cassette not recognised: reinsert the cassette until it clicks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No paper: the cassette is empty, replace it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Paper jam: open the cover, remove the jammed label, reinsert the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cover open: close the cover."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Warming up, cooling down, cleaning: wait, printing continues by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Swipe the panel to cut: the label was printed without cut, swipe across the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pale colours, yellow tint: old paper (see the cassette's age), or [[ui:Normal]] instead of [[ui:Vivid]]. With old cassettes try [[ui:Brightness]] −1 to −3 under [[ui:Colour adjustment]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Background barely visible: ZINK hardly prints very light pastel shades, choose a medium shade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stripes: clean with the CK-1000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content cut off at the edge or askew: increase the [[ui:Safety margin]], insert the cassette straight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:content scaled down to fit]]: the fixed length is too short. Make it longer or use [[ui:Automatic length]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Something else? [[ui:Report a problem…]] in the main menu (also offered with error messages) opens a prefilled issue in the browser with version, system and printer. You see everything before sending it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Design and print"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Elements are placed one after another along the tape. Order them with [[ui:Move up]] and [[ui:Move down]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Editing a text element](media/expand.png#only-light)  ![Editing a text element](media/expand-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Text**: any installed font, colour, several lines. [[ui:Size]] 0 fills the tape height, otherwise fixed in pt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Image**: photos and graphics; drag and drop works too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Code**: QR code, Code 128 or EAN-13."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Automatic length]]: the label is as long as its content. Off: fixed [[ui:Length]], content aligned and scaled down if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Spacing]]: space at the ends and between elements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Edge spacing]]: extra space along the tape edges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Background colour]], [[ui:Background image]]: printed edge to edge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Border]]: width, 0 = none; always inside the safety margin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Units]]: millimetres or inches, by default from the system language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Safety margin]] (printer setting, default 1.5 mm): content and border keep this distance from the tape edges. The printer loses about 0.5 mm per side, and long labels can run up to 1 mm askew. If text is cut off at the edge, increase it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Print dialog](media/print.png#only-light)  ![Print dialog](media/print-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Copies]]: number of labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Cut]]: [[ui:Full cut]] separates the labels. [[ui:Half cut]] cuts through the label, the backing holds them together. [[ui:No cut]]: the printer waits, swipe its panel to cut."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Colours]]: [[ui:Vivid]] for the strongest colours, [[ui:Normal]] (Brother: Standard) for softer ones, black and white (400 lpi) for text and codes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Colour correction: brightness and colour balance (red, green, blue), for this print only, not stored in the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Export PNG…]] saves the label as image."
msgstr ""
